            section("Thread safety", "`conmap` synchronizes individual stripe operations. Other mutable maps contain no container-level synchronization. Persistent node reference counts permit shared-node lifetime management across independently owned versions; publication, assignment, movement, or destruction of the same container handle still requires synchronization. Thread safety also depends on the selected allocator and on key/value operations."),
